%% aoneahsan-cccs-firebase — full flow
flowchart TD
    trigger([Firebase work]) --> task{What are you doing?}

    task -->|choosing a product| boundary{Which product?}
    boundary -->|Auth, Firestore,<br/>Hosting, Analytics| allowed[Allowed — free tier]
    boundary -->|Cloud Functions| nofn[NOT ALLOWED — needs the paid<br/>Blaze plan. Use a Cloudflare Worker]
    boundary -->|Cloud Storage| nostore[NOT ALLOWED — use FilesHub]
    boundary -->|capacitor-firebase<br/>crashlytics/performance| nobanned[BANNED. Sentry for errors,<br/>native/Amplitude for perf]

    task -->|deploying| deploy{Which command?}
    deploy -->|--only firestore| destructive[🔴 NEVER. It deploys rules AND<br/>indexes as a unit — an index missing<br/>from your local file is DELETED]
    destructive --> safe
    deploy -->|--only hosting| safe
    deploy -->|--only firestore:rules| safe
    deploy -->|--only firestore:indexes| safe
    safe[Safe. Pre-authorised for<br/>projects under code/]

    task -->|wiring auth| platform{Which platform?}
    platform -->|web| popup["signInWithPopup +<br/>GoogleAuthProvider"]
    platform -->|native| codetrix["codetrix google-auth for the idToken,<br/>then signInWithCredential — so both<br/>platforms land the SAME Firebase user.<br/>NEVER capacitor-firebase/authentication"]
    codetrix --> serverid{Is serverClientId reaching<br/>the native config?}
    serverid -->|check| envtrap[Verify the GENERATED<br/>capacitor.config.json — this is<br/>exactly the value the env trap<br/>silently blanks]
    envtrap --> ownersetup[google-services.json + SHA-1/256<br/>in the console are OWNER work —<br/>record in docs/MANUAL-TASKS.md]

    popup --> emailpw
    ownersetup --> emailpw
    emailpw{Adding email/password?}
    emailpw -->|for the product UI| noemail[NO. Google-only]
    emailpw -->|for automation testing| devhook[DEV-only, UI-less hook.<br/>Dynamic import under import.meta.env.DEV.<br/>Absence from dist/ is a BUILD GATE]

    task -->|config| envcfg[Web config is client-public by design,<br/>but still lives in .env with a<br/>boot-time check so a misconfigured<br/>deploy fails LOUDLY]

    task -->|analytics| sink[One service, three sinks.<br/>Skips providers lacking keys]
    sink --> native{Running natively?}
    native -->|yes| adid[It reads the advertising ID —<br/>declare AD_ID in the manifest AND<br/>the Play declarations AND Data Safety]
    native -->|no| done

    allowed --> done
    nofn --> done
    nostore --> done
    nobanned --> done
    safe --> done
    noemail --> done
    devhook --> done
    envcfg --> done
    adid --> done
    done([Verify, then deploy])

    classDef gateNode fill:#fff4e6,stroke:#d97706,color:#7c2d12
    classDef terminal fill:#ecfdf5,stroke:#059669,color:#064e3b
    classDef warn fill:#fef2f2,stroke:#dc2626,color:#7f1d1d
    class task,boundary,deploy,platform,serverid,emailpw,native gateNode
    class trigger,done terminal
    class destructive,nofn,nostore,nobanned,noemail warn
